#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\n- $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\n- $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b8ca444-6c66-54ed-845f-78a70554ec28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284283} {:answer/id #uuid "0818345a-ed06-5552-ba9c-5204a8c6abfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284284} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f8e967-74b3-57af-bf45-28e2793f20e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284285} {:answer/id #uuid "67c014cb-d190-5071-83f1-5c2a13627f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284286} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0793b8-872b-5d21-8f1c-c8c8f7cb3f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b8ca444-6c66-54ed-845f-78a70554ec28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284283} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5def946-074f-51ba-aec2-408a7d0b5170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1b62d90-2496-5af6-bac3-452acf9abda8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130269" :question/problem "Calculate $BA+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B(A+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA+BC & =B(A+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} {:answer/id #uuid "84a1361a-1e8e-5442-b48f-b8c533733c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284291} {:answer/id #uuid "a73e9be0-a15c-5e95-8efa-ac9158db8bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284292} {:answer/id #uuid "8c675a0b-99ca-5086-8620-c9431c39b740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284293} {:answer/id #uuid "f031a871-3f8b-5f28-bf58-220ac920e602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d147b5f-6d58-5c16-b472-c51cdf38be30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e3975d8-0204-5147-a2bf-df4657a2f13f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130449" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=A{I}_{3}B$\n- $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$\n- ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82dac9ef-b0b4-5b93-94aa-2bebeddc2c56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284297} {:answer/id #uuid "542fed80-23be-5a6a-9fdd-47aa3c2e1b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284298} {:answer/id #uuid "3aac59d5-cc4e-57d8-88a4-356b447d2602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284299} {:answer/id #uuid "e224fd99-46a1-5abf-af6d-eebe5f79fbb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284300} {:answer/id #uuid "fc794510-f10f-5ac1-a703-308df3b39b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "542fed80-23be-5a6a-9fdd-47aa3c2e1b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284298} :answer-field/id #uuid "645d9ca0-1e91-5e12-ac1f-4d79dc2c1b79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19cf732b-11c4-5a7a-98ba-06159f5b2c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130455" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $A(BC)=(AB)C$\n- $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- $CA=AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efda95f0-5dcd-5aff-a3e2-001e3cc26a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284304} {:answer/id #uuid "8c47a968-2571-54a2-885a-ed45df9cd59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284305} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8620b8-2e45-5c76-bbcd-a5670545d92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284306} {:answer/id #uuid "29bb6638-1e62-5371-a72e-5100891d3700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284307} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fab5b-de8d-579a-b91a-92e2fa5dd08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fab5b-de8d-579a-b91a-92e2fa5dd08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284308} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7a7b06-862d-5083-86ca-fda7c303154e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35d12d0a-00b0-5153-a6da-b9f29bfa020a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130478" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $(CA)B=C(BA)$\n- $(A+A)B=2AB$\n- $CB=BC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5465025-1508-59cc-a4ab-0618cbe8be6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284311} {:answer/id #uuid "092c08b7-9c75-583c-9a92-7b3090d1ade1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5465025-1508-59cc-a4ab-0618cbe8be6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284311} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e82af00-b849-5be5-a517-5dedc78f2a54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef0a9732-c583-514b-b128-b3f3293d4042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0a9732-c583-514b-b128-b3f3293d4042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284314} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e494b0-c9ce-521e-b208-c0462f3fb8af" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b755e90f-da36-5f3c-9262-a8e7720fc5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b755e90f-da36-5f3c-9262-a8e7720fc5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284316} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b416ad-2f8e-534e-b914-beab4e34aa9f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfec9c5e-72c5-5924-8826-3fc2c1955ce9" :question/math-academy-id "q-275518" :question/problem "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5} & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $8\\sqrt{5}$ | $-4$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $16$ |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $12$ | $20$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}C \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8\\sqrt{5} & -4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 4\\sqrt{3} & 16 \\\\ -8 & 12 & 20\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319} :answer-field/id #uuid "79136c64-d827-567e-8129-842c22759199" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2babf67-567f-5287-8719-752fb496e896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17