egin{aligned}AC+BC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97387733-f510-5994-8dd6-a8da130337fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284326} {:answer/id #uuid "44c6bfa4-59a7-500f-b8d5-3350b51d6d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97387733-f510-5994-8dd6-a8da130337fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284326} :answer-field/id #uuid "aae2cf12-9f1e-59cf-91df-c47894732160" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "699e2987-5019-5358-b686-86103dff32ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "699e2987-5019-5358-b686-86103dff32ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284329} :answer-field/id #uuid "81157d48-46dd-5197-b396-3d78118dec13" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d458147f-9345-5ebe-a464-a097a91a723d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d458147f-9345-5ebe-a464-a097a91a723d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284331} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb0e8bc5-297c-520b-bcd8-6fa0077c0adc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7c86000-afce-5a81-8566-1058d6015f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7c86000-afce-5a81-8566-1058d6015f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284333} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb902e1-2e1e-56ab-926a-d9f1534f7465" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99775890-adcd-51f0-8298-6dec5c766a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-319922" :question/problem "Calculate $AC-BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC-BC=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $-4$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} | $4$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law on the right:\n\n$$\nAC-BC=(A-B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, compute $A-B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC-BC & =(A-B)C \\\\  & =(4{I}_{3})C \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4f8f3f2-f2e9-5d09-a854-78edc7b7baa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f8f3f2-f2e9-5d09-a854-78edc7b7baa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284336} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b570fa3-72c2-5f55-81d6-ae0bb06bbf80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2104c358-58e3-5f20-a163-71281139f15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2104c358-58e3-5f20-a163-71281139f15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284338} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b46c9a9-afd0-56ba-be3b-1cfb4e741c5e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9f715ba-feac-55d0-99f0-0e365b187cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f715ba-feac-55d0-99f0-0e365b187cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284340} :answer-field/id #uuid "f709ce3d-b369-563e-a497-8cf0e17d7488" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f9ab189-3c3f-545e-b1e3-3d9c6e402fbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-320021" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 48 & -60\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cbcf2da-e996-5a8b-860a-aafce6954cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284343} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f62552-7f4f-5a6f-a001-f601c000d2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284344} {:answer/id #uuid "c190782d-1973-5aaa-8f88-3e28701c95ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284345} {:answer/id #uuid "258bfa2d-a48c-5056-8ae9-76b8d70f3893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284346} {:answer/id #uuid "54bbf7dd-9203-553e-adea-251bf86bde4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cbcf2da-e996-5a8b-860a-aafce6954cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284343} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac1dd74-37e7-5475-b2e1-0327e8b3a4c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54c6b58b-7b12-5b44-8e47-3a85c2ee0cea" :question/math-academy-id "q-41981" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "678b2272-7810-5f56-a6ac-c62a10f854fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284350} {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} {:answer/id #uuid "761fb85b-7392-51f2-a63e-085c9a729140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284352} {:answer/id #uuid "881f57bb-479b-5b8e-8d7f-0c549e81b862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284353} {:answer/id #uuid "087bc156-bdfb-592d-896a-4cca3f807665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} :answer-field/id #uuid "e140af37-5d21-52b2-9992-47ed85fb2f2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638edf80-8d70-51f1-a06b-07cfe064f004" :question/math-academy-id "q-42001" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e42f31-ce99-56b3-a1be-a057ca8ca9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284357} {:answer/id #uuid "d625c701-2a09-57dc-80a3-3c8a8cdac641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284358} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0ed742-e1f6-5663-99d9-1c72bc05efc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284359} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1300f1-da6c-54d4-9bf5-43b4a440058b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284360} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4746b8-8929-5ea4-ba22-0392651e3c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 30 & 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25e42f31-ce99-56b3-a1be-a057ca8ca9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284357} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2b9f858-7dcf-5f42-8200-6e0474bc0024" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1320ce80-071b-5207-9487-c1aca0bbdba8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42002" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4ba81a-30af-5f74-8a3a-41bbba49b9f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 15 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284364} {:answer/id #uuid "632f1952-6cb3-5c38-a37f-9a2f88abe36e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284365} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0d0f94-648d-5cf1-9547-8127d86e0147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -15 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284366} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b2d3e-c2ef-573f-81aa-57a64db1941b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284367} {:answer/id #uuid "6afb5fc9-7206-5106-8439-2fdb34add402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6afb5fc9-7206-5106-8439-2fdb34add402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284368} :answer-field/id #uuid "8249c7fd-5dab-5669-baea-b63bbbd60bb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72c2951d-d6a9-5cec-b270-d342a8fcfdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42259" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4850773c-6bcc-551d-a93f-540191d439c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284371} {:answer/id #uuid "388c0e33-3ef1-5ea5-be12-9bbc891b7836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284372} {:answer/id #uuid "41f62b05-a630-515b-869f-ec26f26dee89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284373} {:answer/id #uuid "81287a0c-d4ef-5472-9ae6-6338c1ca4de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284374} {:answer/id #uuid "16f86846-2d61-5b4e-b5f2-c0547f0bf49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16f86846-2d61-5b4e-b5f2-c0547f0bf49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284375} :answer-field/id #uuid "ede7a744-1463-5430-afe6-82b73ff42681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c442c42-8f2f-5dfb-989e-15ebcb2f116e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42264" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=BA$\n- $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a051e9-615d-5a50-a282-bff34c7c16e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284378} {:answer/id #uuid "7e805fb9-aa02-5856-8112-843cde035385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284379} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca157dc-147d-540e-9749-22b509872430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284380} {:answer/id #uuid "077f2322-1f5c-5980-b3ab-e7385960d58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284381} {:answer/id #uuid "aa169583-c312-5ca4-af40-927d15f44ccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58a051e9-615d-5a50-a282-bff34c7c16e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284378} :answer-field/id #uuid "29de7b83-7106-5dcb-94e1-ef84c75d8680" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f92d8dd-9d19-55c9-8b9c-e4887c95c7ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-75635" :question/problem "Calculate $CB+CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nCB+CA=C(B+A).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+A$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB+CA & =C(B+A) \\\\  & =C\\cdot 4{I}_{3} \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0d8c0eb-c319-51a4-a17e-f56d510bc0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284385} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b77e69-9143-52f6-929e-21e9530bfe09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284386} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb35f8f-7051-5ce1-8621-d135bd9b5aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284387} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d67cec-9d74-504d-b1e1-bf1726dd6ad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284388} {:answer/id #uuid "820d6eae-5d69-5e49-a182-6b166f05af51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0d8c0eb-c319-51a4-a17e-f56d510bc0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284385} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3120bf-85b5-5f3c-a60d-1683aa03a755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a49601e3-1a30-5183-8bcf-fc2cbb86c6be" :question/math-academy-id "q-75664" :question/problem "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $4\\times 4$ matrices,  and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n- $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A{I}_{4}=AB+A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II  and III are true."}]}
